(48,566 real changes made, 48,566 to missing)

.         replace pglabnet = .    if  pglabnet  <= 0
(28,166 real changes made, 28,166 to missing)

. 
.         * German (dummy variable if the nationality is German)
.         gen             Germany = 0             

.         replace Germany = 1     if      pgnation == 1
(60,403 real changes made)

.         
.         * Transformation of labour income into logs (Note: There seems to be 
> a problem when using net labour income pglabnet)
.         gen     log_pglabnet = ln(pglabnet)
(42,798 missing values generated)

. 
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * 
. 
.         * We test for the effect of having at least one daughter (d_daughter)
>  on political 
.         * preferences (plh0004) using a panel regression model with fixed eff
> ects at the 
.         * individual level. We ommit variables that do not vary at the indivi
> dual level across time, 
.         * (female, nationality, religion or East-German). In addition, we do 
> not include the level of 
.         * education (pgisced11) because this is only available in 2014 and 20
> 19 (including this variable
.         * implies that we no longer have a panel becuase the number of observ
> ations and groups coincide). 
.         
.         xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2005 to 2019, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         xtreg plh0004 d_daughter age age2 i.pgfamstd i.pgemplst log_pglabnet 
> i.syear, fe cluster(pid)
note: 2019.syear omitted because of collinearity.

