.         
.         * NOTE: In H2 we test for the effect of having daughters on political
>  preferences. Our PAP specifies that we will control for the same variables a
> s in H1. Some of these controls are automatically excluded from the analysis 
> when we conduct a panel regression model with fixed effects at the individual
>  level; in particular, female, nationality, religion or East-German do not va
> ry at the individual level across time, thus the regression analysis omits th
> ese variables. In addition, we noted that the education level cannot be inclu
> ded in the analysis because this variable (pgisced11) is only available in 20
> 14 and 2019. If we include the level of education we no longer have a panel b
> ecause we will get the same number of observations and groups; i.e., there wi
> ll only be one observation per group. 
.         
.         
.         
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * 
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[d_daughter] / _se[d_daughter]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 scalar coef_d_daughter = _b[d_daughter]

.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
.         // Display the saved statistics
.         di "Coefficient: `coefficient'"
Coefficient: -.1266231424478028

